From 7eae7b3d403fad9acb937bab9e5335ea824da7af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:17:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(serve): every chat-hosting backend is discoverable for
 plugin activation, not just the role holder [daveey]

The host rendezvous keeps one record per role. Two Desktop-owned backends can run at once: the
supervised always-on SSH backend (`hermes serve --isolated`, launchd com.hermes.always-on-dashboard)
and a local Desktop pool child, or two pool children. Both claim `desktop-serve`; the loser returns
on HELD_BY_OTHER and publishes nothing, and never re-claims when the holder exits. On daveey-mini
the always-on backend on :9147 (hosting the MacBook Desktop's chats over SSH) lost the record to a
pool child at 22:46; once that child exited only `host-desktop-serve.lock` was left, so
`hermes plugins enable` and hermes-sync's backend activation reached only serve:9119 and :9147 kept
its old plugin hooks (t_01a1ce929e118cf2).

- gateway/host_backends.py: each serve backend also publishes `serve-backends/<pid>.json` (a
  HostRecord) + 0600 `<pid>.token`, whatever its role-lock outcome. Readers trust an entry only while
  its pid names the same incarnation (start ticks + boot epoch) and prune provably dead ones; the
  entry is removed on exit (atexit + SIGTERM via host_rendezvous.register_exit_cleanup).
- plugins_activation.serve_backend_records(): role records first, then token-consistent entries not
  already listed (dedupe pid/port). notify_serve_backend_record dials with the record's own entry
  token, else its role token only when the role record names the same pid.
- Discovery only: the attach/refuse ladder still reads role records; an entry never makes a
  backend a host owner.
---
 gateway/host_backends.py                      | 177 ++++++++++++++++++
 gateway/host_rendezvous.py                    |  25 ++-
 hermes_cli/plugins_activation.py              |  17 +-
 hermes_cli/web_server.py                      |   7 +
 tests/gateway/test_host_backends.py           | 100 ++++++++++
 ...lugin_activation_second_desktop_backend.py | 117 ++++++++++++
